course: dictionary
lesson: 7414
title: Poky and small rooms
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words describe a place, and the sentence around them tells you how it feels. «Alice thinks Mabel lives in a poky little house» with next to no toys. The clues show that poky means small and cramped, with not much room to move.
explain: Check whose idea it is. Alice only guesses about Mabel's house, so the reader learns what Alice thinks, not what is true. Ask yourself: is this a fact, or someone's guess? Context can give you the meaning of a word, and it can also show you whether a character is right.
explain: Poky also has an informal American meaning: slow and dull. Use the context to choose the right sense. A house is a place, so small and cramped fits best there.
fact: Poky means small and cramped, with not enough space.
fact: «A poky little flat» is a flat with very little room.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Mole's home, Mole End, is small but cosy, and Mole worries the Rat will think it poky and shabby.
fact: Poky is informal, so you will hear it in everyday talk more than in formal writing.
fact: In American English, poky can also mean slow and dull.
exercise: Alice thinks Mabel lives in a «poky little house». What does poky mean here? | Very old and made of stone | *Small and cramped, with not enough space | Large, with lots of rooms and a garden | Bright and sunny
exercise: Alice has only guessed about Mabel's house. What does this tell you? | Alice has visited Mabel many times | Mabel has lots of toys | *Alice may be wrong, because it is only her guess | Mabel definitely lives in a poky house
exercise: Mole worries the Rat will think his home is poky. What does Mole fear? | That the Rat will think it is too big | That the Rat will want to move in | *That the Rat will think his small home is cramped and shabby | That the Rat will never visit
test: «The poky room had no space for a sofa.» What does poky mean? | *Small and cramped | Big and bright | Fresh and airy
test: In American talk, a film that is poky is one that is slow and dull. Which meaning of poky is this? | Small and cramped | Fast and exciting | *Slow and dull | Full of noise
exam: Which meaning of poky fits «a poky little flat»? | Slow to answer | *Small and cramped | Shiny and new | Very quiet and calm
